The path: view, intention, and ethical conduct (@buddhist-path-and-conduct: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @buddhism, #source @buddhist-source-eightfold-path, #philosophy @buddhist-attention-and-concentration, #buddhism @buddhist-attention-and-concentration) { r_57VHYWATNTSTMPRY0PBMWRR6CS
**Read:** the preface and chapters I–IV of [The Noble Eightfold Path](../sources/Eightfold-path.lingua#r_5CE3K4AJC79ZEQPJVRD2QRDY0P). Start with ordinary reading ability. A nikāya is a collection of discourses; a sutta is a discourse. The Dhamma here names the teaching and the way it describes, not merely a set of opinions to assent to.

The eightfold path joins view and intention with speech, action, livelihood, effort, mindfulness, and concentration. Its training concerns how one understands, acts, and cultivates attention. Ethical conduct is already part of this beginning; it will not first appear when we reach social questions.

Follow the account of kamma, intentional action, alongside the discussion of view and intention. Distinguish an action, its motive, and an account of its consequences. An assertion about kamma does not by itself establish that a particular person’s suffering is deserved; such an inference would require its own textual and argumentative support.

**Work with an example:** choose a truthful statement that could nevertheless be cruel or poorly timed. Separate accuracy, intention, foreseeable effect, and the circumstances of speaking. Use Bodhi’s account to explain which considerations matter. Do not turn a single example into a complete definition of right speech.

**Check:** explain the threefold grouping of ethical conduct, concentration, and wisdom, and why those groups support one another. Distinguish understanding an instruction from having cultivated the quality it describes.

**Continue:** [Effort, mindfulness, and concentration](Attention-and-concentration.lingua#r_74GC8WHWYR6VPR27ZMP3D94T59).

**Return:** [Buddhism: from the path to sustained inquiry](../Buddhism.lingua#r_7P61Z6HHZNZZ8ND3DHXSFSNRRE).
